S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sudhakar</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaiphei</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Retained surgical sponge: an unusual cause of intestinal obstruction</article-title><source>J Clin Gastroenterol</source><year>1997</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>57</fpage><lpage>58</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9013355</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00004836-199701000-00014</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nosher</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Siegel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Percutaneous retrieval of nonvascular foreign bodies</article-title><source>Radiology</source><year>1993</year><volume>187</volume><fpage>649</fpage><lpage>651</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8497610</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaiser</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name><name><surname>Friedman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Spurling</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><name><surname>Slowick</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaiser</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The retained surgical sponge</article-title><source>Ann Surg</source><year>1996</year><volume>224</volume><fpage>79</fpage><lpage>84</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8678622</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00000658-199607000-00012</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>